    {
      "id": "story-004",
      "authorId": "user-001",
      "authorName": "Amara Diallo",
      "authorAvatar": "https://i.pravatar.cc/150?u=amara",
      "authorLocation": "Zurich, Switzerland",
      "title": "Building Generational Wealth",
      "summary": "How our family tontine is creating a legacy",
      "content": "In Senegal, my grandmother ran a tontine for 40 years. When I moved to Switzerland, I missed that sense of community and shared purpose. CircleUp let me recreate that tradition digitally. I started a family circle with my siblings and cousins across three countries. We've completed two full cycles, and the funds have helped start a small business, pay for a wedding, and build savings for the next generation. My children now understand the value of community and collective prosperity. This is more than saving money - it's preserving our culture.",
